      <title>When a Single Rain Gauge Speaks for the Planet: How a Narrow Dataset Becomes a Global Climate Headline</title>
      <link>https://wattsupwiththat.com/2025/12/07/when-a-single-rain-gauge-speaks-for-the-planet-how-a-narrow-dataset-became-a-global-climate-headline/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=when-a-single-rain-gauge-speaks-for-the-planet-how-a-narrow-dataset-became-a-global-climate-headline</link>
      <description>If there is one robust trend visible here, it is not in rainfall but in rhetoric: the persistent escalation from modest signal to grand conclusion. Until that trend reverses, the distance between climate data and climate discourse will continue to grow—and with it, public confusion about what the numbers truly mean.</description>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">https://wattsupwiththat.com/2025/12/07/when-a-single-rain-gauge-speaks-for-the-planet-how-a-narrow-dataset-became-a-global-climate-headline/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=when-a-single-rain-gauge-speaks-for-the-planet-how-a-narrow-dataset-became-a-global-climate-headline</guid>
      <pubDate>Sun, 07 Dec 2025 22:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
    </item>
